            <ArticleTitle>The Risk of M. tuberculosis Transmission from Pediatric Index Cases to School Pupils.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/INF.0000000000001492</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study is the largest report on M. tuberculosis transmission rate (TR) from children with pulmonary tuberculosis to school pupils. Higher TR (around 21.6%) was observed in contacts of smear-positive children. TR from pediatric smear-negative index cases was around 0. If our data are confirmed, school contacts of a smear-negative index case could be screened only by clinical evaluation and TST, avoiding routine use of chest radiographs in children less than 5 years of age as well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
